  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an integer NNN.\n\nConsider an integer XXX (1≤X≤N)(1\\le X \\le N)(1≤X≤N). In one move, you have to:\n\n\nRandomly pick an integer P(1≤P≤N)P (1 \\le P \\le N)P(1≤P≤N);\nSet the value of XXX to gcd(X,P)(X, P)(X,P).\nLet, E(X,N)E(X, N)E(X,N) denote the expected number of moves required to make X=1X = 1X=1.\n\nFind the value of E(X,N)E(X, N)E(X,N) for all 1≤X≤N1\\le X \\le N1≤X≤N.\n\nThe value can be represented as an irreducible fraction PQ\\frac{P}{Q}QP​, where PPP and QQQ are coprime integers. You need to output P⋅Q−1P \\cdot Q^{-1}P⋅Q−1 modulo (109+7)(10^9+7)(109+7), where Q−1Q^{-1}Q−1 represents the multiplicative inverse of QQQ modulo (109+7)(10^9+7)(109+7).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input will contain a single integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint NNN space separated integers, the values of E(X,N)E(X, N)E(X,N) for all 1≤X≤N1\\le X \\le N1≤X≤N.\n\n\nThe value can be represented as an irreducible fraction PQ\\frac{P}{Q}QP​, where PPP and QQQ are coprime integers. You need to output P⋅Q−1P \\cdot Q^{-1}P⋅Q−1 modulo (109+7)(10^9+7)(109+7), where Q−1Q^{-1}Q−1 represents the multiplicative inverse of QQQ modulo (109+7)(10^9+7)(109+7).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\le N\\le 5\\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105"
    ],
